// case: route-limits-past-32-are-refused-not-dropped
// what: 33 routes declare a limit. The runtime table holds 32
//      (ADMISSION_MAX_ROUTE_LIMITS, runtime/admission.h), and past it
//      orbit_admission_register_route_limit counts a drop and returns, so the
//      server starts and serves that route under the global gate instead of
//      the policy the source declared. The checker refuses the program.
// expect-error: route limits, and 32 is the most the server can enforce
route GET "/r01" limit 1 / s { return ok 200 "x" }
route GET "/r02" limit 1 / s { return ok 200 "x" }
route GET "/r03" limit 1 / s { return ok 200 "x" }
route GET "/r04" limit 1 / s { return ok 200 "x" }
route GET "/r05" limit 1 / s { return ok 200 "x" }
